values ('b2c3d4e5-6f7a-4c41-8e01-1f2a3b4c5d11', 'multicultural-postcolonial-literature', 'Multicultural / Postcolonial Literature', 'Students establish the field''s key terms, stakes, and reading practices across multicultural, postcolonial, ethnic, diasporic, and transnational literary study. The course examines how empire produced knowledge and representation, how anti-colonial writing imagines resistance and decolonization, and how nation, language, race, diaspora, Indigenous sovereignty, the Black Atlantic, borderlands, gender, memory, genre, global markets, critical methods, and scholarly ethics shape comparative literary analysis.');

