ts"}, {"id": "54c40c7a-878a-40d9-958a-6230399316a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Competing readings"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn to apply theory through passages rather than dropping jargon onto texts."}]}, {"id": "79f28b51-ba3c-480c-9b22-705ef3266acb", "type": "topic", "title": "Research, Secondary Sources, and Scholarly Ethics", "description": "Build responsible research habits for working with criticism, archives, historical context, and community-sensitive materials.", "children": [{"id": "ba3afc08-b1ae-430c-b39a-e2c1d360755b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Finding scholarly conversations", "children": [{"id": "64147756-e680-4aef-a86b-0675c725d84b", "type": "concept", "title": "MLA International Bibliography"}, {"id": "3d07a058-7a96-4783-adfd-626ea134e5c5", "type": "concept", "title": "JSTOR"}, {"id": "fd583af2-6a85-4bb9-9f89-dec97d16dc26", "type": "concept", "title": "Project MUSE"}, {"id": "e7466edf-c665-4942-a651-fba3bd84ef81", "type": "concept", "title": "Oxford Bibliographies"}], "description": "Gist: Students use research tools to locate field-specific criticism and debates."}, {"id": "04461a4b-4245-4f7d-8715-6484eb9b6a9a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using sources ethically", "children": [{"id": "e6a41382-c982-4b94-b0ab-f5c574059da8", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation"}, {"id": "dd2da2b3-be84-48b6-bc16-faa972a73509", "type": "concept", "title": "Paraphrase"}, {"id": "ee6ba6cf-8a49-4d44-8064-6b9048c468a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Context"}, {"id": "567bf0f7-d103-499a-b63c-04807cb897d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding extraction"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn to represent scholars, communities, and histories carefully."}, {"id": "e9cd773e-a239-4d78-8041-3e746325f37b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research design", "children": [{"id": "bbc179e4-f5b9-4302-afab-ff277b875097", "type": "concept", "title": "Research question"}, {"id": "3b5f0bc5-65a8-46eb-ab90-1d32a5d53981", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotated bibliogra